JBRD-metadata wiring via new zenjpeg API — task #10 (2026-05-28)
====================================================================

Goal
----

Close 2 known-DIFF cases on the jpeg-in-jxl recompression bench by
exposing per-block `extra_zero_runs` + per-scan `reset_points` from
zenjpeg's entropy decoder so jxl-encoder's JBRD writer can populate
`JpegScanInfo.extra_zero_runs` and `JpegScanInfo.reset_points`
correctly. These match libjxl's `JPEGScanInfo` fields per
`enc_jpeg_data_reader.cc:849-857`.

Scope
-----

  - New zenjpeg 0.8.5 API: `Decoder::decode_coefficients_with_jbrd_metadata()`
    returns `(DecodedCoefficients, JbrdMetadata)`. Existing
    `decode_coefficients()` and `decode_coefficients_with_extras()`
    are unchanged — zero overhead, no tracking.
  - jxl-encoder switches `extract_coefficients_zenjpeg` to the new
    API; merges per-scan `reset_points` + `extra_zero_runs` into
    the marker-scanner-built `scan_info` by bitstream order with a
    spectral-parameter sanity check.

Encoders / decoders
-------------------

  ours    = cjxl-rs from this repo at HEAD plus the path-pinned
            zenjpeg sibling workspace at
            `../zenjpeg--jbrd-metadata-api/zenjpeg` (= zenjpeg 0.8.5).
  djxl    = libjxl djxl v0.12.0 d2c7032 (`--reconstruct_jpeg`
            via file-extension auto-detect).
  jxl-rs  = third-party jxl-rs `jxl_cli` (PNG decode only, used to
            verify pixel-level reconstruction round-trips even when
            we cannot byte-roundtrip — both task files decoded
            cleanly to PNG, confirming bitstream validity).

